      <activity id="ad30b735-7aa0-5bcd-b814-6ba0e6e99c4e" activityNameId="28682900-9c94-57eb-9021-77d5b9448a1b" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Electricity, at cogen 1MWth, biomethane, economic allocation</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Electricity, at cogen 1MWth, biomethane, economic allocation
Inventory for 1 MJ heat from biomethane, burned in a cogeneration unit with a capacity of 1MWth. The multioutput process "biomethane, burned in cogen 1MWth delivers the coproducts "heat, at cogen 1MWth, biomethane, allocation exergy" and "electricity, at cogen 1MWth, biomethane, allocation exergy". The energy efficiency is 41% for electricity and 47% for heat. The economic factor is 0.72 for electricity and 0.28 for heat. This leads to the allocation factor of 0.69 for electricity and 0.31 for heat.;
Synonyms: Strom, ab BHKW 1MWth, Biogas, aufbereitet, ökonomische Allokation; 
UUID: 5bf0320e-ad8f-3f17-82cb-33fd82fd60e7
Included are the biomethane burning in a 1 MWth cogen unit which in turn includes fuel input, infrastructure (boiler), air and water emissions and electrictiy needed for operation. The efficiency and economic allocation is considered
Location: Data apply to the combustion in Switzerland.
Technology: efficiency of average technology available on the market
Time period: Time of publications.
Production volume: na
Sampling: Data from literature 
Extrapolations: &lt;null&gt;
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_5bf0320e-ad8f-3f17-82cb-33fd82fd60e7.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
